{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Third main-green defect, and this one was MINE: terraform fmt on monitoring_9ea3.tf\n\nThe tightened monitor fired FAILED(post-fix, ACTIONABLE) on 'Terraform Drift' -- a workflow neither\nof the known blockers touches, so it was worth looking at immediately. Its plan job failed at\n'terraform fmt -check' (exit 3) naming infra/terraform/monitoring_9ea3.tf, a file I added earlier this\nsession for bug 9ea3.\n\nCause: alarm_name padded for alignment against a neighbour that is a COMMENT; terraform does not\nalign across comments. One line, whitespace only.\n\nTHE PART WORTH KEEPING: the fmt step runs FIRST, so the PLAN JOB NEVER RAN. The Drift workflow has\nnot been checking for actual infrastructure drift at all -- a whitespace defect silently disabled the\nentire point of the workflow. That is the FOURTH instance today of one shape: something did not\nexecute, and the surface presented as a normal failure that nobody traced to 'the real work never\nstarted'. The others: 9a17 (a worker kill presenting as a crash, hiding a timeout), 90c7 (a job that\nnever ran, yet its change still got Verified +1), 337e (a browser tier that never runs, reported as\ngreen). I now treat 'what did NOT run in this job' as a first-class question rather than reading only\nwhat failed.\n\nFixed and pushed as change 2614. fmt -check -recursive now clean.\n\nCommitted under 9ea3's trailer rather than opening a new ticket: 9ea3 is in_progress and mine, the\ndefect is in its own file, and a fresh ticket plus a 15-20 minute plan-review for a one-line\nwhitespace fix is ceremony without information. Reasoning recorded on the ticket so the trailer does\nnot read as scope creep.\n\nALSO ENCOURAGING: main has advanced to 6b034b9f8224 'Make scanner-integration recipe POSIX-sh\nportable' -- the owning session is actively fixing the blocker. Once it lands, the plan is to rebase\nall five held changes in one batch."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788504137141546001,"uuid":"8befb6c6-bf37-4948-a434-8937a538a8e8"}